{
 "name": "units-slice-tree-derives-from-relations",
 "acceptance_item": 2,
 "note": "R3c's second acceptance item, at the tier that owns the data half: the slice tree is DERIVED from member-of edges and is not a `depth` member on a row (the R1 ruling). Two levels resolve — services to system.slice, system.slice and machine.slice to the root — so a consumer holding these relations can build the tree without the collector having flattened it into a coordinate that would be wrong the moment a row was sorted or filtered. The fifth edge names a slice this host does not publish and stays unresolved, carrying its name: a unit whose slice is not here is a real reading, and dropping the edge would render identically to a unit with no slice at all. The RENDERING half of this item — indentation disabled under sort or filter — is a page, and the page is R4's; what is judged here is that the data a page needs exists and is derived rather than declared.",
